WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:05.400
Movies are big business, and major studios
earmark their spots on the release schedule

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.779
years ahead of time.

00:00:06.779 --> 00:00:11.740
As such, it isn't too early to start making
box office predictions for 2018.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.390
There are dozens of promising projects slated
for release, so here are some of the movies

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:19.620
that are going to blow everyone away in 2018.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.620
Han Solo

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:25.490
Now that Rogue One has proven that the Star
Wars galaxy is viable even without Jedi, the

00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:30.560
Han Solo prequel, with Alden Ehrenreich taking
over the role from Harrison Ford, has sturdier

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.279
legs than R2D2.

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:38.280
The film, co-directed by Phil Lord and Christopher
Miller, co-stars TV's Emilia Clarke and Donald

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:42.640
Glover, and looks to shed light on how Han
became such a swaggering space scoundrel in

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.640
the first place.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:47.699
Han Solo's faithful fans should be eager to
see a story from his younger days.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.920
But the big question remains — will we finally
get to meet Chewy's family on the big screen?

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:55.840
(Wookie roars)

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.600
Hopefully, the answer's a resounding "no."

00:00:58.609 --> 00:01:01.300
We'll find out on May 25, 2018.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.120
Avengers: Infinity War

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.040
If we had to pick a shoe-in for smash of the
summer, it'd have to be Infinity War.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.730
The MCU has really all been building up to
this moment.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:14.640
Iron Man and his Avengers, the Guardians of
the Galaxy, Spider-Man, Doctor Strange, and

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.280
Captain Marvel — everyone's gonna be there
for the big battle's beginning.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:22.790
This is the blockbuster of the year, no doubt
about it, and it launches on May 4, 2018.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:24.470
The Predator

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:29.480
Kicking off a new round of interplanetary
big game hunting, The Predator finds writer-director

00:01:29.480 --> 00:01:34.210
Shane Black — who was one of Arnold's fellow
soldiers in the 1987 original — making a

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:37.000
long-overdue return to the franchise.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:42.210
Black's promised to make it "the biggest Predator
yet" on February 9, 2018, with the help of

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:45.980
sci-fi savvy stars Boyd Holbrook and Olivia
Munn.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:47.050
Bad Boys for Life

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:52.090
By the time Bad Boys for Life hits theaters,
a full 15 years will have passed since Bad

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:57.010
Boys 2, when detectives Mike Lowrey, played
by Will Smith, and Marcus Burnett, played

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:00.470
by Martin Lawrence, decided that they were,
well...

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:02.100
"Bad boys for life."

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:06.530
It's a bromantic sentiment which is obviously
true if they've survived another decade and

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:07.840
a half together.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.560
Little is known about what the duo will be
getting into this time, but if it's anything

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.569
like the first two films, it's bound to escalate
quickly.

00:02:14.569 --> 00:02:19.990
"Now back up, put the gun down, and give me
a pack of Tropical Fruit Bubblicious."

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.310
"And some Skittles."

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:24.490
Pacific Rim: Uprising

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:29.990
The domestic receipts for 2013's Pacific Rim
were a bit of a disappointment, but the Guillermo

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:34.840
del Toro film was well-liked by those who
actually ventured out to see the stylish sci-fi

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:35.840
showcase.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.590
Even though the lackluster North American
ticket sales of the first film seemed to put

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:44.170
the idea of a follow-up in the "unlikely"
column, international audiences, always ready

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:48.870
for a monster fight, gave producers enough
motivation to justify greenlighting a second

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.040
round of the Kaiju smackdown.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:56.220
John Boyega joins the cast as the son of Idris
Elba's character from the first installment.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:59.849
Expect a release on February 23, 2018.

00:02:59.849 --> 00:03:01.220
Ant-Man and the Wasp

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:05.630
For many, Ant-Man was one of the most enjoyable
entries in the MCU to date.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:09.849
The tiny title character, played by Paul Rudd,
was as earnest as they come, and the Honey

00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:13.730
I Shrunk the Kids-esque visual spectacle of
the movie was just pure fun.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:19.220
The final act set the stage for Hope van Dyne,
played by Evangeline Lilly, to finally suit

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.000
up alongside our hero.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:25.170
So for those who've relished the Wasp's adventures
in the comics, it's about time we get to see

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.170
her fly.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:28.810
And at least we know that Ant-Man survives
Infinity War, right?

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.569
We'll find out on July 6, 2018.

00:03:31.569 --> 00:03:33.239
Wreck-It Ralph 2

00:03:33.239 --> 00:03:37.459
Disney's Wreck-It Ralph was a commercial and
critical success that found a way to entertain

00:03:37.459 --> 00:03:40.770
kids and parents nostalgic for the 8-bit era.

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:45.370
We know John C. Reilly and Sarah Silverman
will return to voice their unlikely heroic

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:50.450
duo, but all that's been revealed so far is
that it'll be released on March 9, 2018, and

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:53.840
Ralph will be "wreaking havoc on the web"
this time around.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:57.739
And we already know that Reilly is an Internet
expert, so we're in good hands.

00:03:57.739 --> 00:04:00.380
"In 1971, Bill Grates invented Michaelsoft.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:05.870
Wouldn’t it be cool if I could remember
my DINGUS password for my email?

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:08.209
That would be cool!"

00:04:08.209 --> 00:04:09.209
Black Panther

00:04:09.209 --> 00:04:14.270
The Marvel Cinematic Universe is expanding
even further in Phase Three, with Ryan Coogler's

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:19.280
Black Panther branching out to Wakanda to
focus on Chadwick Boseman's T'Challa, who

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.000
made his debut in 2016's Captain America:
Civil War.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:28.410
With an all-star cast that includes Oscar-winner
Lupita Nyong'o and Danai Gurira, along with

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:33.970
frequent Coogler collaborator Michael B. Jordan,
Black Panther is poised to continue the MCU's

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:38.310
streak of box office domination on February
16, 2018.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.310
Aquaman

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:44.160
The brief introduction of Arthur "Aquaman"
Curry in Dawn of Justice was but a taste of

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:48.460
what's to come from Game of Thrones' Jason
Momoa as the trident-wielding hero, who'll

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:51.910
embrace his destiny as the heir to the kingdom
of Atlantis.

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:56.680
Director James Wan helms the wet and wild
action film, set for release on October 5,

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:01.540
2018, with Amber Heard, Patrick Wilson, and
Willem Dafoe also on deck to star.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:04.500
Thankfully, there are no green stretch pants
in sight.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:05.500
Tomb Raider

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:10.199
Even without Angelina Jolie back for another
round of archaeological badassery as Lara

00:05:10.199 --> 00:05:14.650
Croft, the Tomb Raider reboot-slash-prequel
should fare nicely with recent Oscar winner

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:17.160
Alicia Vikander stepping into the lead role.

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:22.460
On March 16, 2018, the new film will take
viewers back in time into an earlier chapter

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:23.790
from the character's history...

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.200
"Well...kill her!"

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:28.360
"Hey!"

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:35.439
Okay, maybe not that early.

00:05:35.439 --> 00:05:39.770
Croft will on a search for her father and
Walton Goggins is coming on to play the villain.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.310
The Incredibles 2

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:45.650
Disney-Pixar's The Incredibles was a blast,
but writer-director Brad Bird took a long

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:49.270
break before getting down to work on a second
installment.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:53.620
Details on the sequel are slim, but with our
live-action comic heroes mostly just fighting

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:57.930
with each other lately, it might be prime
time to offer up a return to good old-fashioned

00:05:57.930 --> 00:05:59.020
villain-fighting.

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:03.540
If you're looking for a semi-sequel before
the film's release on June 15, 2018, you can

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:06.960
always dig out your GameCube and play Rise
of the Underminer.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:08.389
Jurassic World Sequel

00:06:08.389 --> 00:06:13.229
After what happened in 2015's Jurassic World,
it might be hard to envision a scenario that

00:06:13.229 --> 00:06:16.810
would allow the world's deadliest theme park
to legally reopen for business.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:21.670
But the film's box office domination made
a sequel a legal requirement.

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:25.420
While we can't even guess what they'll get
up to this time around, we know stars Chris

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:31.020
Pratt and Bryce Dallas Howard are expected
to reprise their roles on June 22, 2018.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:32.540
That, and there'll be a lot of action figures.

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:35.860
"And a pteranodon battles a spitting dilophosaurus!

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:37.290
Each sold separately!"

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:38.720
Mission: Impossible 6

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:41.479
Tom Cruise's Ethan Hunt is at it again.

00:06:41.479 --> 00:06:45.680
Director Christopher McQuarrie returns to
helm a sixth installment of the covert ops

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:47.300
action-adventure series.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:51.699
While details are minimal as to what the actual
storyline will be, Cruise has promised that

00:06:51.699 --> 00:06:56.460
some bonkers new stunts he's spent years training
for will be among the many set pieces.

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:59.680
Get ready for action on July 27, 2018.

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:00.710
A Wrinkle In Time

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:06.120
Amazingly, the cherished sci-fi-fantasy children's
classic has yet to be adapted to death by

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:09.680
Hollywood, and we're not counting the 2003
Disney Channel movie.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:14.610
So for director Ava DuVernay, the sky itself
isn't even a limit as to what she can do with

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:15.910
this beloved tale.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:20.680
She's brought in a boatload of A-listers to
help her bring the saga to the silver screen,

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:25.690
including Reese Witherspoon, Chris Pine, and
professional weirdo Zach Galifianakis.

00:07:25.690 --> 00:07:28.770
Put some time aside on April 6, 2018.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:30.419
The Flash

00:07:30.419 --> 00:07:34.710
The DC Extended Universe gives Ezra Miller
his turn to shine here in a standalone turn

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:39.740
as Barry "The Flash" Allen, after the character
was introduced in Batman V Superman: Dawn

00:07:39.740 --> 00:07:40.770
of Justice.

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:45.789
The small screen has been kind to the speedy
hero with The CW's The Flash, but maybe not

00:07:45.789 --> 00:07:48.000
so kind to 1990's Flash…

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:56.650
...so there's really no way to know which
kind of Flash we'll get, especially now that

00:07:56.650 --> 00:08:00.840
the creative team on the film has changed
multiple times, and the script has returned

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:02.040
for a complete rewrite.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:06.780
Still, there's a good chance fans will race
to the ticket stand in 2018 for this one.

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:07.780
Jungle Book

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:13.900
Not to be confused with Disney's animated
1967 classic, or the 1994 live-action film,

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:19.480
or even Jon Favreau's live-action version
from 2016, or the slew of other adaptations

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:23.900
inspired by Rudyard Kipling's book about a
boy who's raised by jungle animals…

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:29.770
Andy Serkis' version of The Jungle Book, anticipated
for release on October 19, 2018, will feature

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:35.500
him in prime motion-capture form, alongside
sci-fi fantasy mainstays Benedict Cumberbatch,

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:38.130
Christian Bale, and Cate Blanchett.

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:40.370
Fantastic Beasts and Where To Find Them 2

00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.370
J.K.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:45.300
Rowling's Harry Potter spinoff series Fantastic
Beasts and Where to Find Them is on deck for

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:50.170
its second installment, following Eddie Redmayne's
Newt Scamander and his pals on another leg

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:52.950
of his adventure through American Witchcraft
and Wizardry.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:57.330
Following the first film's introduction of
Gellert Grindelwald, played by Johnny Depp,

00:08:57.330 --> 00:09:01.480
and a mention of Albus Dumbledore, the second
film is expected to begin the battle for the

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:05.410
ages between the esteemed professor and his
former bestie-gone-rogue.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:08.720
The film launches on November 16, 2018.

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:10.300
Mary Poppins Returns

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:11.300
Author P.L.

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:15.110
Travers might be rolling in her grave over
this one, but there's reason to believe the

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:21.230
new installment of the Mary Poppins story
could recapture some of the magic of the supercalifragilisticexpialidocious

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:23.380
nanny and her now-grown charges.

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:28.990
Emily Blunt stars in the title role, with
Emily Mortimer, Ben Whishaw, Colin Firth,

00:09:28.990 --> 00:09:30.980
and Lin-Manuel Miranda supporting.

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:36.180
Dick Van Dyke is also expected to appear in
the film, but at over 90 years old, he won't

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:39.510
be climbing up any rooftops or cleaning chimneys
anytime soon.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:42.640
Get ready for a spoonful of Poppins on Christmas,
2018.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:44.000
Avatar 2

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:49.440
James Cameron has buzzed about a sequels to
his 2009 alien adventure Avatar for ages,

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:54.180
and after years of much hype and delay, it's
finally, probably, maybe actually happening.

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:59.790
Sam Worthington and Zoe Saldana are expected
to reprise their roles as the formerly interspecies

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:05.180
romantic partners Jake and Neytiri, and somehow
Sigourney Weaver is also going to be involved,

00:10:05.180 --> 00:10:07.360
despite the death of her character.

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:11.560
But she's also hinted that the pic might just
get pushed back again beyond its expected

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:14.720
December 21, 2018 release date.

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:16.670
Maze Runner: The Death Cure

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:22.010
Production on the third Maze Runner installment
was significantly delayed back in April 2016

00:10:22.010 --> 00:10:26.810
due to a gruesome injury suffered by lead
actor Dylan O'Brien on the set.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:31.300
Despite that setback and a middling domestic
box office return on the first sequel, The

00:10:31.300 --> 00:10:36.720
Scorch Trials, the series' third run at the
big screen should kick off on January 12,

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:40.310
2018 — nearly a year after its planned release
date.

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:44.700
But its promise to finally give those gladers
their big showdown with WCKD should be enough

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:49.470
to give audiences their second wind and get
them out for the franchise's finish line.

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:50.470
Ready Player One

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:54.810
While young adult dystopias haven't all done
well at the box office lately, Ernest Cline's

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:58.640
bestselling novel has all the components to
make it a solid success.

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:02.860
Combine an engrossing Willy Wonka and the
Chocolate Factory-meets-Hackers narrative,

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:08.050
with a strong cast including Ben Mendelsohn,
T.J. Miller, and Olivia Cooke, and blockbuster

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:11.670
director Steven Spielberg, and you have a
recipe for success.

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:14.269
Start getting ready on March 30, 2018.

00:11:14.269 --> 00:11:18.590
If it's anything like the book, it'll be an
amazing trip back to the '80s.

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:21.900
(whipping it good)

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:23.380
Rampage

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:25.970
Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson just can't seem
to miss lately.

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:30.780
So with him on deck to star in this adaptation
of the classic arcade game about giant monsters

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:35.490
destroying city skylines for the heck of it,
it doesn't actually matter that it's a ridiculous

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:36.490
concept.

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:40.220
Johnson will reunite with director Brad Peyton
— the same pairing that brought box office

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:45.740
glory to 2012's Journey 2: The Mysterious
Island and 2015's San Andreas.

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:50.230
Get ready for giant apes and killer lizards
on April 20, 2018.

00:11:50.230 --> 00:11:51.649
How The Grinch Stole Christmas

00:11:51.649 --> 00:11:55.820
Apparently, we haven't seen the last of Dr.
Seuss' Christmas-stealing character.

00:11:55.820 --> 00:12:00.460
While Jim Carrey's turn as the holiday-hating
beast was enough to satisfy the live-action

00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:05.720
crowd, Universal Pictures is rebooting the
original on November 9, 2018, with Benedict

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:09.940
Cumberbatch lending his vocals to the title
role, because the first two movies on this

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:12.010
list starring Cumberbatch just weren't enough.

00:12:12.010 --> 00:12:13.370
Ladies love the Cumberbatch.

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:17.089
"He was so close that had he been wearing
cologne, I think I would have been able to

00:12:17.089 --> 00:12:18.269
tell.

00:12:18.269 --> 00:12:22.300
Just the lightest Cumbermusk in the Boston
sunshine."

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:25.660
Deadpool 2

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:30.310
Ryan Reynolds made a triumphant return as
Wade "Merc with a Mouth" Wilson in Deadpool

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:34.209
after appearing as the mutilated character
in X-Men Origins: Wolverine.

00:12:34.209 --> 00:12:38.589
The unexpected departure of director Tim Miller
is a little troubling, but Reynolds remains

00:12:38.589 --> 00:12:43.310
dedicated to the franchise, and he's indicated
that the sequel might bring a mutant mercenary

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:48.250
named Domino on board for the next round of
action, as well as one more early reveal…

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:49.790
"The sequel?

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:50.930
We're gonna have Cable."

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:52.040
Thanks for watching!

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.790
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.240
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

